# Profiles: a radio's settings with the radio taken out, made from a backup and put on any radio
# of the same firmware.
#
# First the making, on the backup's own screen: the parts it offers, all ticked, two left out,
# and a name. Then Settings > Profiles: the two on the card - one for each firmware, so the one
# for the other firmware says why it cannot be compared - and a .cfg from a phone to read in.
# Then one profile, compared with the radio on the link and applied.
scene demo
clock 2026-09-29 14:20
delay 160
config
backups list
profiles list

# Backups is two rows above About; its connected radio, and that radio's newest backup.
tab settings
key down 24
key up 2
key a
key down
key a
key down
key a
hold 1200

# "Make a profile" is under the backup's facts. The picker reads the backup first.
key down 40
key up 2
hold 1200
key a
hold 700
profiles draft
hold 2400

# Position and Bluetooth left out: this is for another radio in the same place on the mesh.
key down
key a
profiles tick 1
hold 700
key down 5
key a
profiles tick 6
hold 1600

# Named, starting from the radio's own name.
key down 40
hold 900
key a
hold 2000
key start
hold 1400
toast Profile saved: Ridge relay
hold 1800

# Out to the Settings list, and into Profiles, the row above About.
key b
hold 500
key b
hold 500
key b
hold 700
key down 24
key up
key a
hold 2600

# The Meshtastic one: what it sets, and what can be done with it.
key down
key a
hold 2400
key down 40
hold 1600
key up 2
hold 900

# Compared with the radio: only its parts can differ.
key a
hold 900
profiles compare
hold 3200

# Applied: the sheet, then the profile going on, then the radio read back and matching.
key down
hold 900
key a
hold 2800
key up
key a
profiles applying
hold 2200
profiles same
hold 2200

key b
hold 900
key b
hold 1400
